  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program Budgeting and Fiscal Risk Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This project builds on the previous capacity development project (PCC-405525 Budget Execution and Controls, Cash Management, Government Accounting, and Fiscal Risks) implemented by the IMF between 2018 and 2023.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This technical assistance (TA) project supports the Guinean Ministries of Budget and Economy and Finance in the implementation of its public financial management (PFM) reforms priorities. It aims at strengthening practices in three crucial areas of public financial management: (i) the implementation of program budgeting and further roll-out of climate and gender budgeting, (ii) fiscal reporting, and (iii) fiscal risks management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is organized around 2 strategic objectives:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Strategic objective 1: Strengthened budget management&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Strategic objective 2: Improved coverage and quality of fiscal reporting&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It will delivered via a long-term resident advisor embedded at the General Directorate of Budget and short-term missions by IMF&apos;s HQ staff and independent consultants.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
